 ORDER OF PARAMETERS IS AS FOLLOWS:
 
 AS1=FIRST ADJUSTED SPOT
 AS2=SECOND ADJUSTED SPOT
 
  (1) - AS1 LATITUDE
  (2) - AS1 LONGITUDE
  (3) - AS1 ANGULAR RADIUS
  (4) - AS1 TEMPERATURE FACTOR
  (5) - AS2 LATITUDE
  (6) - AS2 LONGITUDE
  (7) - AS2 ANGULAR RADIUS
  (8) - AS2 TEMPERATURE FACTOR
  (9) - A=ORBITAL SEMI-MAJOR AXIS in Solar radii
 (10) - E=ORBITAL ECCENTRICITY
 (11) - PERR0=ARGUMENT of PERIASTRON at time HJD0 in radi ans
 (12) - F1=STAR 1 ROTATION PARAMETER
 (13) - F2=STAR 2 ROTATION PARAMETER
 (14) - PHASE SHIFT= PHASE OF PRIMARY CONJUNCTION
 (15) - VGAM=SYSTEMIC RADIAL VELOCITY
 (16) - INCL=orbital inclination in degrees
 (17) - g1=STAR 1 GRAVITY DARKENING EXPONENT
 (18) - g2=STAR 2 GRAVITY DARKENING EXPONENT
 (19) - T1=STAR 1 AVERAGE SURFACE TEMPERATURE in 10000 K
 (20) - T2=STAR 2 AVERAGE SURFACE TEMPERATURE in 10000 K
 (21) - ALB1=STAR 1 BOLOMETRIC ALBEDO
 (22) - ALB2=STAR 2 BOLOMETRIC ALBEDO
 (23) - POT1=STAR 1 modified surface potential
 (24) - POT2=STAR 2 modified surface potential
 (25) - Q=MASS RATIO (STAR 2/STAR 1)
 (26) - HJD0= Hel. JD reference time
 (27) - PZERO= orbital period in days at time HJD0
 (28) - DPDT= dimensionless time derivative of orbital pe riod (e.g. days/day)
 (29) - DPERDT= time derivative of argument of periastron in radians per day
 (30) - a3b=relative semi-major axis for 3rd body orbit in Solar radii
 (31) - P3b=3rd body orbit period in days
 (32) - i3b=inclination of 3rd body orbit to plane of sky in degrees
 (33) - e3b=eccentriicity of 3rd body orbit
 (34) - omega3b=argument of periastron of 3rd body orbit in radians
 (35) - T03b=HJD of superior conjunction of inner system center of mass with regard to the outer orbit
 (41) - log d= log (base 10) of distance in parsecs
 (42) - A_desig = interstellar extinction in designated photometric band
 (43) - onset time of spot 1
 (44) - start time of constant maximum for spot 1
 (45) - end time of constant maximum for spot 1
 (46) - end time of spot 1
 (47) - onset time of spot 2
 (48) - start time of constant maximum for spot 2
 (49) - end time of constant maximum for spot 2
 (50) - end time of spot 2
 (56) - L1=STAR 1 RELATIVE MONOCHROMATIC LUMINOSITY
 (57) - L2=STAR 2 RELATIVE MONOCHROMATIC LUMINOSITY
 (58) - X1=STAR 1 LIMB DARKENING COEFFICIENT
 (59) - X2=STAR 2 LIMB DARKENING COEFFICIENT
 (60) - el3=third light
 
